<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>


<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">Among
the outstanding restricted share units brought forward from December 31, 2020, 1,499 restricted shares were vest in May 2022. The remaining
restricted share units will vest in February 2029, upon fulfilment of requisite service period by the employees.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">On
October 10, 2022, the Company granted and issued 225 shares of restricted Class A Ordinary Shares to three non-executive directors as
their compensation for the year from March 1, 2022. The restricted shares were vested in a straight-line method over the service period,
and will be transferable after a lock-up period of six months. As of December 31, 2022, 188 share were vested. The grant-date value of
each restricted share units was $92.8 by reference to the closing price on October 10, 2022, and the total fair value of these restricted
Class A Ordinary Share units aggregated $20,880.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"></P>

