<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">NOTES TO
UNAUDITED CONDENSED CONSOLIDATED FINANCIAL STATEMENTS</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">As
of June 30, 2025 and December&nbsp;31, 2024, there was $nil retained earnings in the aggregate, respectively, which was generated by
the Company&rsquo;s VIE and its subsidiaries in Renminbi included in the Company&rsquo; consolidated net assets, aside from 1,391,350
and $1,419,190 statutory reserve funds as of June 30, 2025 and December&nbsp;31, 2024, that may be affected by increased restrictions
on currency exchanges in the future and accordingly may further limit the Company&rsquo;s PRC subsidiary and VIE and VIE&rsquo;s subsidiaries&rsquo;
ability to make dividends or other payments in U.S. dollars to the Company, in addition to $13,111,994 and $13,139,835 restricted net
assets as of June 30, 2025 and December&nbsp;31, 2024, respectively, as discussed above.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><B>15. CONCENTRATION
RISK</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">The
Company has a concentration of its account receivables with specific customers. As of June 30, 2025, four customers accounted for 18.2%,
13.1%, 12.4% and 11.0% of net accounts receivable, respectively. As of December 31, 2024, three customers accounted for 18.4%, 14.4%
and 11.4% of net accounts receivable, respectively.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">For
the six months ended June 30, 2025, four customers accounted for approximately 15.7%, 13.5%, 10.6% and 10.0% of the total revenue, respectively.
For the six months ended June 30, 2024, one customer accounted for approximately 15.9% of the total revenue.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">As
of June 30, 2025 and December&nbsp;31, 2024, the Company had insignificant balance of accounts payable and did not further assess the
concentration risk of accounts payable.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">For
the six months ended June 30, 2025, one supplier accounted for approximately 13.8% of the total cost of service revenue and product purchase.
For the six months ended June 30, 2024, two suppliers accounted for approximately 13.5% and 12.6% of the total cost of service revenue
and product purchase, respectively.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

